   "notes": "cliff / waterfall terrain tile (32 x 32; pool water 1.0 over bed 0.2, channel water 17.4 over bed 17.1, grass top 18.0): a block of big flat-faced rock columns under one lime grass cap split by a river channel that pours over a notch as a three-lobed curtain into a full-width pool; a splash disc with spray spikes, a foam ribbon, foam rings round two boulders; stepped bush-capped columns, low pine boxes, pines, ferns, flowers. One closed land shell plus vegetation, water, curtain and foam shells (three see-through water pieces). Back seam = M034's seam raised 16.4. 16 sockets"
